.cache/

# Copied app bundle (generated by deploy workflow)
docs/assets/app/

# CI output — generated by filter_public_data.py, not source. Except
# survey-status.json: a bare, sorted list of event ids
# with the survey switch on, no personal data -- committed deliberately so
# services/signup-relay can read this repository's own copy through the
# GitHub Contents API, the same credential and the same call shape it
# already uses for instance/keys/events/<id>.pub, rather than depending on a
# deployed example-showcase URL that has never actually been built.
instance/public-data/*
!instance/public-data/survey-status.json
# The internal agenda feed: committed for the identical
# reason survey-status.json is -- `.github/workflows/deploy.yml`'s own
# "Commit internal agenda" step needs a tracked path to commit to. Unlike
# survey-status.json, nothing reads this one over an API; it exists so an
# internal subscriber's calendar client can point at this repository's own
# copy directly. It is never copied into `app/public/` or
# `site/src/_data/` by anything this build runs -- see `tools/convener_ops/
# agenda.py`'s own module docstring for why that absence, not a flag, is
# what keeps it off both published sites. `.gitattributes` marks it binary
# so a checkin never renormalises its own CRLF line endings (RFC 5545's own
# requirement) to this repository's default `eol=lf`.
!instance/public-data/agenda-internal.ics
# The registration lane cutoffs: committed for exactly
# the reason survey-status.json is, and read by exactly the same worker
# through exactly the same Contents API call shape -- one already-resolved
# instant per event, the moment a registration for it stops being far
# enough away to wait for the daily drain. Event ids and timestamps, no
# personal data, no speaker's name; generated by `tools/convener_ops/cli.py::
# registration_routing_public_data` and pushed back here by `.github/
# workflows/deploy.yml`'s own "Commit registration routing" step.
!instance/public-data/registration-routing.json

# Notification body -- a run artefact of convener-notify-*, written only when a
# channel is configured, posted by the notify workflow, never edited.
notify-body.md

# The Actions budget alarm's own body, written by convener-record-actions-usage
# only when a channel is configured *and* something actually fired -- the
# same "the file's existence is the whole signal" shape notify-body.md has,
# on its own filename so that the alarm and the daily digest, composed in
# the same job, cannot overwrite one another.
budget-body.md

# The submission queue alarm's own body, written by convener-record-queue-watch
# only when a channel is configured *and* something actually fired. A third
# filename for the third message this one job can compose, for the reason
# budget-body.md is the second: one filename shared between them means
# whichever is written last silently replaces the rest.
queue-body.md

# What the collector step read from the Actions API, one JSON object per
# line, for tools/convener_ops/maintenance/actions_usage.py to reduce offline. A run
# artefact of a single job; the measurement derived from it is committed to
# instance/data/actions-usage.yml, this raw form never is.
actions-usage-input.jsonl

# The host's short list of attendance to resolve by hand
# (tools/convener_ops/cli.py::match_attendance). Written only when
# attendance.match finds an unmatched or unreachable attendee. Never
# committed regardless -- and this comment no longer says "never
# printed", because that scope covered
# stdout, not the 14-day build artefact this file was already being
# uploaded as, which is exactly where the leak was. The file itself no
# longer carries a name or an address either way (see
# UNMATCHED_ATTENDANCE's own comment in cli.py); kept ignored as
# defence in depth, not because its content still needs it.
unmatched-attendance.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
tools/.venv/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.coverage

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Local credentials. Never committed: the real values live in GitHub Secrets,
# and a copy on disk is only ever for trying something out.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Event private keys (tools/convener_ops/journey/eventkeys.py never writes one to disk --
# this guards a human trying one out by hand). Only the published .pub half
# belongs in instance/keys/events/.
*.pem
instance/keys/events/*
!instance/keys/events/*.pub

# Certificate signing private key (tools/convener_ops/journey/signing.py never writes one
# to disk either). Unlike instance/keys/events/, every .pub ever committed here stays
# forever -- rotation retires a key from service, never from this directory
# -- but the rule protecting the private half from an accidental commit is
# the same one. instance/keys/signing/README.md documents the layout and is exempted
# below so the directory's contract survives even while it holds no keys.
instance/keys/signing/*
!instance/keys/signing/*.pub
!instance/keys/signing/README.md

# Raw attendance export (tools/convener_ops/journey/platform.py::ManualPlatform). Contains
# personal data -- display names and addresses off the meeting platform --
# and is dropped here only for one read, never committed. The room link and
# join instructions come from instance/data/speakers.yml and instance/data/config.yml instead
# (`platform.find_speaker`), never from a file under this directory. This filename-specific
# pattern deliberately does not reach instance/data/events/<id>/registrations.enc or
# instance/data/events/<id>/survey-responses.enc (tools/convener_ops/journey/registration.py and
# survey.py) -- both *are* committed, and both hold nothing but
# per-record ciphertext, the opposite of what this rule exists to keep out.
# Nor does it reach instance/data/events/<id>/attendance-import.csv.enc
# (tools/convener_ops/journey/platform.py::encrypt_attendance_export) -- the same trick
# played a third time: encrypted under the event's own public key, which
# needs no secret to produce, and committed, so a CI job holding the
# matching private key can read it even though the plaintext this rule
# excludes can never reach a checkout at all.
instance/data/events/*/attendance-import.csv

# The designer's own source material for the visual identity -- the .pptx the
# brand values were extracted from, and the rendered examples. Reference only,
# never published and never committed: several of these carry a real person's
# photograph, which is exactly the defect docs/assets/flyer-example.png
# already put in this history. Kept out of git so a stray `git add` cannot
# repeat it. Read them from the Drive working copy.
docs/assets/example_and_template_initial_assets/
